        "execSummary":  "Enterprise leaders deploying AI decision-support tools should note that adding explainability features may backfire: a multi-university study shows that LLM-generated rationales cause evaluators to defer to AI reasoning rather than exercise independent judgment, producing worse outcomes than unexplained AI recommendations alone. This directly challenges the prevailing assumption that explainable AI is always better AI. For customer-support and operations leaders, this means oversight workflows that present AI reasoning alongside recommendations may undermine the human-in-the-loop value they are designed to provide. The implication is to pilot stripped-down AI outputs before investing in expensive explainability layers.",
